    "editorial": {
      "title": "Qubole-linked credentials expose forgotten AWS integration roles",
      "summary": "Wiz and Sentra’s November 9 disclosures describe attackers using Qubole-associated AWS credentials to assume customer integration roles, collect secrets and access S3 data. Wiz dates the observed activity to October 14–26; this is a new disclosure of older activity.",
      "why_it_matters": "Dormant vendor trust can remain usable after an integration stops being used. An External ID did not prevent the observed role assumptions.",
      "action": "Inventory and remove unused vendor trusts. Review unusual role assumptions and S3 object reads, limit integration-role permissions, and investigate exposed secrets.",
